English
In short
QR Labels does not collect any personal data, requires no account, contains no ads or analytics, and sends nothing to any server. All data stays on your device.
Who operates the app
Pavel Zachar, contact: pavel.zachar@icloud.com
What data the app works with
The app stores on your device only what you enter yourself:
labels you create and their contents (phone numbers, addresses, links, contacts, Wi-Fi network names, account numbers and payment amounts),
boxes and the lists of items in them, including the change history,
templates,
optional personal details (name, phone, email) that are prefilled into new labels.
Wi-Fi passwords are stored in the iOS system Keychain. All other data is stored in the app's storage on the device.
What the app does not send anywhere
No data is sent to the developer or to third parties. The app contains no ads, tracking, analytics or third-party libraries that collect data.
When data leaves the app
Only as part of an action you take yourself:
you save a label to Photos, print it or share it as an image or PDF,
you export a backup to a .qrlabels file and send it on (for example via AirDrop). The backup file contains all your data, including Wi-Fi passwords in readable form, so send it only to yourself or to people you trust,
you pass data to another app through the system share sheet.
What happens to the data after you send it on is determined by the recipient or the app you choose.
Permissions and system features
Photos (add only): the app only saves finished labels to Photos. It does not read your photos.
Wi-Fi connection (Hotspot): the app joins a network only after you tap the button and confirm the system dialog. It does not monitor or change other networks.
Contacts: the Add to contacts action opens the system sheet with a prefilled contact. The app does not read your contacts.
Shortcuts: the Open Niimbot and Open Smart Banka buttons only run a shortcut that you created yourself. No data is passed along.
Camera: the app does not scan QR codes itself and does not ask for camera access. You scan a box QR code with the system Camera app, which then opens QR Labels.
Device backups
If device backup is turned on (iCloud or computer), iOS may include the app's data in it. Apple manages this backup and you control it through your settings.
Deleting data
You can delete individual labels, boxes and templates directly in the app. Deleting the app removes all its data from the device. iOS may keep Keychain items after the app is deleted, and the app will use them again if you reinstall it.
Children
The app is not directed at children and does not collect any data about them.
Changes to this policy
If the way data is handled changes, I will update this policy and the effective date.
